# Ash Outstanding Extension

```elixir
Mix.install([{:ash_outstanding, "~> 0.2.1"}], consolidate_protocols: false)
```

## Overview

If already familiar with the [Elixir Outstanding Protocol](http://github.com/diffo-dev/outstanding) and [Ash Framework](https://ash-hq.org) in this livebook tutorial you will learn

* Brief Recap of Outstanding Protocol
* Why have an Ash Outstanding Extension?
* How to declare Outstanding on your Ash Resources
* How to use Outstanding with Ash Resources
* How to use Outstanding in Ash Expressions

## Brief Recap of Outstanding

Outstanding is a protocol for checking whether our expectations have been met or exceeded, and/or seeing which expectations are still outstanding. It compares expected and actual, where these can be of any type.

Outstanding protocol defines two functions:

* outstanding?(expected, actual), returning a boolean which is true if anything is outstanding, otherwise false
* outstanding(expected, actual), returning what is outstanding, otherwise nil

## Why have an Ash Outstanding Extension?

Outstanding is about expectations and actuality and is intentionally not implemented on structs (although it can be done easily).
As Ash is used to model your domain declaratively, we want to declare what Outstanding should be concerned about, without having to deal with the details of how.
The Ash Outstanding extension allows you to declare which attributes outstanding should be calculated on

## How to declare Outstanding on your Ash Resources

We'll declare an Ash Resource representing a Service. We'll use an instance for expected, and another for actual. 
Initially the service will have an id, name, state and status, however we are only concerned with implementing outstanding on state and status.

Using the [README](https://github.com/diffo-dev/outstanding/blob/dev/README.md) configure outstanding on the resource below so that it expects state and status.

```elixir
defmodule Service do
  use Ash.Resource,
    domain: nil,
    data_layer: Ash.DataLayer.Ets,
    extensions: [AshOutstanding.Resource]

  outstanding do
    expect [:state, :status]
  end

  actions do
    defaults [:read, :update, :destroy, create: :*]
  end

  attributes do
    uuid_primary_key :id, writable?: true
    attribute :name, :string, public?: true
    attribute :state, :atom, public?: true
    attribute :status, :atom, public?: true
  end
end
```

```elixir
Code.ensure_loaded?(Service)
```

```elixir
expected = 
```
